# Build context is the REPO ROOT for every image in this monorepo.
# pnpm workspaces use `workspace:*` links, so a Dockerfile that only copies its
# own package directory cannot resolve its dependencies. Keep the context lean
# here instead.
#
# node_modules is a named volume at runtime — never copy it into an image.
# .env files are injected at runtime via compose env_file, never built in.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# ⚠ `**/` is required. A bare `dist` matches only the ROOT-level dir in Docker,
#   so host-built packages/*/dist leaked into every image. Local builds then
#   passed on stale output, and a clean checkout (Coolify) has no dist at all:
#   ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND. The Dockerfiles build the workspace packages instead.
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/.svelte-kit
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.cache

.git
.github
.claude

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

coverage
test-results
playwright-report
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts

*.log
*.tgz
.DS_Store

# Local scratch and staging
.staging-identity
media
db-backups
